For the basic feedback control algorithm, we'll use a **Proportional-Integral-Derivative (PID)** controller. The PID algorithm calculates an error value as the difference between the desired and actual motor speeds. It then adjusts the motor speed based on this error, using proportional, integral, and derivative terms to achieve stable control.

